Here is the commit message:
Add block/position convention to all distinct from operators

This commit adds a second implementation to distinct from operator of all
types. This 2nd implementation uses block/position convention. As a
result, for certain types, it's no longer necessary to extract the value
out of the Block in order to invoke "distinct from" operator. This is
expected to resolve performance issue previously introduced in
baad26e68401151cebb2b989404768dfcf093287 (which was work around with a
hack).

Here is the root cause:
The root cause of the bug was a performance issue related to the "distinct from" operator, which required extracting values from blocks before performing comparisons. This extraction process introduced inefficiencies, particularly when handling large datasets, leading to slower performance. The new implementation using block/position convention allows for direct comparisons without the need for value extraction, thus resolving the performance bottleneck.

